  "context": "Feature batch: validation-core. Design source: spec-faithful validation plan, section 'One roll-up rule'.\n\n2026-11-26 staging state: branch feat/staging-crr-v1 at b46cbf2b07 (worktree /Users/joe/Developer/BenchBox.wt-staging-crr-v1), includes the shared roll-up commit 5f99ae81c6 and the Dask distributed-setup test fix. Contained in feat/staging-crr-v2. Next: validation-core batch after the corpus rule PR merges.",
  "description": "## Problem\nFour places roll row evidence up to summary.validation differently: the writer reads only measurement rows (benchbox/core/results/builder.py ~442-457, query_status.py ~139-190); the bundle validator reads every row including warm-ups (benchbox/validation/bundle.py ~3094-3175); the DataFrame summary has its own ladder (benchbox/core/dataframe/query_validation.py ~113-126); the corpus rule has its own predicate (corpus_rule.py ~645-657). A synthetic bundle the writer would call passed was rejected by the validator with 927 errors.\n\n## Change\nOne stdlib-only function in benchbox/core/results/query_status.py returns (status, reason), used by the builder, the bundle validator, the DataFrame summary and row_counts_checked:\n1. Any FAILED evidence on a measurement or warm-up row gives failed (failed queries without FAILED evidence keep partial). The qualification input is added by crr-v4.\n2. Measurement and warm-up rows are judged alike.\n3. passed needs at least one measurement row PASSED by an exact, invariant, range or must-return-rows check, and every other row PASSED or SKIPPED with a documented reason.\n4. No reference for the run's benchmark, scale and data stamp gives no_reference (plus 'reference data differs' when stamps differ).\n5. Anything else is not_validated.\nThe row_counts_checked definition (a PASSED measurement row and no UNVALIDATED row) does not change.\n\n## Decision gates\n- If the change moves any stored bundle's outcome, stop and report it: the expected snapshot diff is none.\n\n## Guardrails (apply to every step of this plan)\n- Fix the root cause for every platform and benchmark. No rule, check, exception, label or test may name a platform or a version matrix; only the pvm items may name Polars, and only to run and stage that run's files.\n- Never edit a stored result file. Stored outcomes change only through the rule; any change shows in the committed snapshot diff (scripts/corpus_compliance_snapshot.py) and is explained per bundle in the pull request body.\n- No new stored class value. No reader decides anything from benchmark.compliance_class, conformance_class or summary.tpc_metrics.suppressed.\n- One implementation per concept: reuse existing helpers; make duplicate-check-delta stays at +0; no second copy of the rule, the roll-up, the row decision or the qualification comparator.\n- No explanatory comments or docstrings (make comment-policy-check). User-facing changes add a changelog.d fragment; never edit CHANGELOG.md.\n- Heavy work only through make heavy-run, after make heavy-status, with command, maximum run time and log path announced first. No live cloud runs. Never touch the lock, set BENCHBOX_SKIP_TEST_LOCK, BENCHBOX_HEAVY_ADMIT=force or BENCHBOX_HEAVY_WATCHDOG=off.\n- Work in a linked worktree on the step's feature batch. Each batch is one pull request; run the local review before opening it; fix hosted-review findings. If the hosted review cannot complete, split the pull request so a reviewer can read it (owner, 2026-11-24). Never post a stand-in or adjudication, except on published-results pull requests, which follow the owner decision of 2026-11-24: an independent review with no Critical or Required findings, then a stand-in that cites it.\n- Paths and line numbers were read on 2026-11-25 at the corpus rule head; re-read before editing and report drift instead of guessing.\n- At a decision gate, follow the recorded owner decision. If its stop condition is met, stop and report to the owner; never substitute a different decision.\n- Owner decisions: crr-00-corpus-rule-remediation-plan context, entries of 2026-11-22, 2026-11-24 and 2026-11-25. Design: the spec-faithful validation plan summarized in crr-00 (qualification test, integrity checks, official-mode sequence).",
